  "id": "terror-management-theory",
  "term": "terror management theory",
  "definition": "Terror management theory is a social psychology framework for understanding how awareness of death and other existential threats can shape attitudes and relationships between groups. It proposes that reminders of mortality can increase preference for one’s own group and negative reactions toward outsiders or criticism of one’s country.",
